  NOT ESTABLISHED against the in-run control.

  Two claims must be kept apart here:
   (a) ATTAINABILITY. clamp reaches beta = 2.0000 and |det| =
       1.0000 exactly; sigmoid tops out near 0.998 and never
       reaches 1. That is the open-vs-closed interval showing up
       numerically, and it holds in every run.
   (b) LEARNING. Attainability does NOT imply the task is
       learned. Runs have reached |det| = 1.0000 and still scored
       at chance, while a run that solved it sat at 0.69. Do not
       cite |det| as evidence the cell trains.
  Next candidates, in order of cost:
    1. curriculum on the demand mixture (low frac(D=max) first --
       the trainability table says that regime trains reliably)
    2. grow K by inserting a beta=0 factor into a trained K-1
       model -- our construction proof says that embedding is exact
    3. orthogonality regularisation on the transition matrices

